win32u, winemac, wined3d: a display mode a program asks for is emulated in a Space

Found with Portal (Direct3D 9, exclusive full screen at 960x600). With full screen in a Space
of its own or as a borderless window (FINEWINE_FULLSCREEN=space|borderless), a program that
set a display mode still changed the Mac's real one: every other window on the Mac was
resized, the display was captured, and the game's picture sat in a corner. Restoring the mode
failed afterwards ("No matching mode found 3024x1898").

dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
- In those two modes Wine's display mode emulation is on (EmulateModeset): the mode a program
  asks for is emulated and its picture brought to the size of its window. Direct3D 10/11 and
  Vulkan pictures are upscaled by MetalFX as before (DXMT, MoltenVK); OpenGL ones, which
  Direct3D 9 and older are, by Wine's own blit. FINEWINE_EMULATE_MODES=0 turns it off.
- A scaling ratio that does not fit two 16-bit numbers is shortened instead of stopping the
  program with an assertion: a program may now ask for any size (1366 wide on a 3024 wide
  display at 192 DPI did not fit).

- FINEWINE_DPI_AWARE=1 runs a program as DPI aware whether it says so or not (Windows:
  "Override high DPI scaling behaviour: Application"). FineWine sets it for games. Portal goes
  full screen through SDL, which sizes the window itself: not DPI aware, in a prefix with 192
  DPI, it was told a screen half the size of the modes it was offered, and its window came
  out twice the screen.

dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
- A "raw" client surface, which is what win32u asks for when it scales the picture itself,
  has the size it has on the monitor. The Mac driver gave every surface the program's size,
  so the scaled blit went past the surface and a corner of the picture was seen, magnified.

dlls/wined3d/swapchain.c
- The window of an exclusive full-screen swap chain is sized to the mode in real pixels. A
  program that is not DPI aware, in a prefix with a high DPI, counts in larger units: in its
  terms the window came out twice the size of the screen it saw, and the pointer reached a
  quarter of it.

dlls/win32u/window.c
- With an emulated mode, a picture that would be larger than the real screen is fitted to it.

Checked with Portal itself (its main menu fills the Space at 3024x1898) and with
tests/runtime/d3d9-fullscreen.c as x64 and 32-bit, in Direct3D's exclusive mode and SDL's way: 960x600 fills the Space,
1024x768 is centred with bars at the sides, the pointer set to the middle of the program's
screen is at the middle of the Space, and the Mac's display mode does not change.

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -320,9 +320,22 @@
 static struct ratio make_ratio( UINT num, UINT den )
 {
     UINT d = gcd( num, den );
-    struct ratio r = { num / d, den / d };
-    assert( num / d < 65536 );
-    assert( den / d < 65536 );
+    struct ratio r;
+
+    /* FineWine: a ratio is kept as two 16-bit numbers, and upstream stops with an assertion
+     * when a size does not reduce that far (1366 wide on a 3024 wide display at 192 DPI does
+     * not). A program may ask for any size, so the fraction is shortened instead: the error
+     * is below one part in 30000. */
+    num /= d;
+    den /= d;
+    while (num >= 65536 || den >= 65536)
+    {
+        num = (num + 1) / 2;
+        den = (den + 1) / 2;
+    }
+    if (!den) den = 1;
+    r.num = num;
+    r.den = den;
     return r;
 }
 
@@ -6153,9 +6166,33 @@
         emulate_modeset = IS_OPTION_TRUE( buffer[0] );
     /* FineWine: a render size for the prefix is an emulated display mode (see add_modes) */
     if (finewine_render_scale()) emulate_modeset = TRUE;
+    /* FineWine: with full screen in a Space of its own or as a borderless window
+     * (FINEWINE_FULLSCREEN, see winemac.drv) the Mac's display mode is never changed for a
+     * program: a mode it asks for is emulated, and what it draws at that size is brought to
+     * the size of its window. Changing the real mode resized every other window on the Mac,
+     * took the display away from macOS, and left a game that asked for a small mode
+     * (Direct3D 9 games in exclusive full screen do) in a corner of the screen.
+     * FINEWINE_EMULATE_MODES=0 turns this off. */
+    {
+        const char *fullscreen = getenv( "FINEWINE_FULLSCREEN" ), *emulate = getenv( "FINEWINE_EMULATE_MODES" );
+        if (fullscreen && (!strcmp( fullscreen, "space" ) || !strcmp( fullscreen, "borderless" )) &&
+            !(emulate && emulate[0] == '0'))
+            emulate_modeset = TRUE;
+    }
 
 #undef IS_OPTION_TRUE
 
+    /* FineWine: FINEWINE_DPI_AWARE=1 runs a program as if it had declared itself DPI aware
+     * (Windows: "Override high DPI scaling behaviour: Application"). FineWine sets it for
+     * games. A game that is not DPI aware, in a prefix with a high DPI (a Retina prefix has
+     * 192), is told a screen half the size of the display modes it is offered, and sizes its
+     * full-screen window by the mode: twice the screen (Portal, through SDL). Games count in
+     * pixels; scaling a program that is not DPI aware is for desktop programs' sake. */
+    {
+        const char *aware = getenv( "FINEWINE_DPI_AWARE" );
+        if (aware && aware[0] == '1') NtUserSetProcessDpiAwarenessContext( NTUSER_DPI_SYSTEM_AWARE, 0 );
+    }
+
     if (app_compat_flags)
     {
         if (strstr( app_compat_flags, "HIGHDPIAWARE" )) NtUserSetProcessDpiAwarenessContext( NTUSER_DPI_SYSTEM_AWARE, 0 );
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/window.c b/dlls/win32u/window.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -347,7 +347,36 @@
 
     get_win_monitor_dpi( hwnd, &raw_dpi );
     *monitor_rect = map_dpi_rect( rect, dpi, raw_dpi );
+
+    /* FineWine: with an emulated display mode, a window larger than the screen it thinks it
+     * has would be given a picture larger than the real screen, most of it out of sight.
+     * Direct3D 9's exclusive full screen does this for a program that is not DPI aware in a
+     * prefix with a high DPI: the window is sized to the mode in the program's own units,
+     * which are larger. No picture is larger than the screen: it is fitted to it, keeping
+     * its shape. */
+    if (emulate_modeset)
+    {
+        RECT screen = get_virtual_screen_rect( no_dpi, MDT_RAW_DPI );
+        int screen_w = screen.right - screen.left, screen_h = screen.bottom - screen.top;
+        int w = monitor_rect->right - monitor_rect->left, h = monitor_rect->bottom - monitor_rect->top;
 
+        if (screen_w > 0 && screen_h > 0 && w > 0 && h > 0 && (w > screen_w || h > screen_h))
+        {
+            if ((INT64)screen_w * h <= (INT64)screen_h * w)
+            {
+                h = (int)((INT64)h * screen_w / w);
+                w = screen_w;
+            }
+            else
+            {
+                w = (int)((INT64)w * screen_h / h);
+                h = screen_h;
+            }
+            monitor_rect->right = monitor_rect->left + max( 1, w );
+            monitor_rect->bottom = monitor_rect->top + max( 1, h );
+        }
+    }
+
     /* use toplevel visible rect relative position, so drivers can then assume it */
     OffsetRect( monitor_rect, monitor_rects.client.left - monitor_rects.visible.left,
                 monitor_rects.client.top - monitor_rects.visible.top );
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
@@ -1147,7 +1147,12 @@
     if (drawable && drawable->client)
     {
         struct macdrv_client_surface *surface = impl_from_client_surface(drawable->client);
-        RECT rect = surface->client.virtual_rect;
+        /* FineWine: a raw surface is one win32u scales into itself (an emulated display mode:
+         * it draws the program's picture at its own size off screen and blits it to this
+         * surface at the size it has on the monitor), so the surface has the monitor's size.
+         * Upstream takes the virtual size here always; the blit then reached past the surface
+         * and only a corner of the picture was seen, magnified. */
+        RECT rect = surface->client.raw ? surface->client.monitor_rect : surface->client.virtual_rect;
         macdrv_make_context_current(context->context, surface->cocoa_view, cgrect_from_rect(rect));
         return;
     }
diff --git a/dlls/wined3d/swapchain.c b/dlls/wined3d/swapchain.c
